    "final_text": "The audit is complete. The review found three low-severity problems, all fixed in commit `7c210d9`:\n- **License:** `package.json` declared an MIT license that nobody chose, with no LICENSE file. I removed the field, so pick a license if you plan to publish.\n- **README:** a heading pointed to a \"spec\" readers don't have and implied it was RFC 4180. It's now \"Edge cases and choices\".\n- **Comment:** a code comment gave the wrong reason for writing a single empty field as `\"\"`. The real reason is that `skipEmptyLines` would drop it.\n\nA second full review of all the changes found nothing new. The full suite passes on the final code (105/105, through `dx run-gate --name full-gate`), and every item in the task is met, with its code and tests listed above.\n\nA few things differ from what the audit asked for:\n- **Review step:** `/dxreview` couldn't be run as a skill here, and its report publisher needs a token only its wrapper provides. I followed its written steps by hand in this session, so no review report was published.\n- **Format, lint, type checks:** none exist in the project, and no formatter, linter or type checker is installed. The only static check was `node --check` on every file.\n\nFive minor points I noted but didn't change:\n- A very long duplicate header name is copied whole into the error message.\n- On Windows with Node 18 or 20, `npm test` relies on the shell to expand the test-file pattern, and Windows' default shell doesn't.\n- The tests need Node 18.6 or later, while `package.json` says `>=18`.\n- Errors for object rows in `stringify` name the field by index, not by column name.\n- There's no option to cap how large a field can grow.\n\nThe work is in four commits on branch `feat/csv-parser`, not pushed because there's no remote. The completion receipt is written.\n\nPROMPT_COMPLETE",
